  "title": "Marking solutions to problems that are not solved",
  "content": "<p><strong>None </strong>of these issues is actually solved:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/66cedb30-c3cd-4723-8472-aa0744771e39.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>The posts marked as the solution are just “We will add this to the list to be considered for improvement”.</p><p>That’s <strong>not</strong> a solution!</p><p>I don’t think a solution should be marked <em>until the issue is actually resolved </em>- whether by fixing the issue, or with a decision that it will not be fixed.</p>",
